SLACKWARE
---------

Slackware and Slackware ARM/AArch64, by Patrick Volkerding and Stuart Winter
respectively, are the distribution this ports. The media is built from
Slackware's own installer, and the installer, setup and pkgtools are used
unmodified except where docs/PORTING.md says otherwise.

  source/slackware-k/sbin/slk-hwm-discover
      Taken verbatim from Slackware ARM's kernel source tree. Stuart Winter's
      copyright notice is intact and must remain so.

Several SlackBuilds here derive from Slackware's own -- notably mesa-asahi and
pipewire-lv2, which take their meson flag sets from Slackware's -- and retain the upstream
copyright notices alongside ours.


ASAHI LINUX
-----------

The Asahi Linux project is the reason any of this is possible. It produced the
Apple Silicon kernel work, m1n1, the U-Boot port, the firmware tooling, and the
audio DSP configuration this port packages:

  linux (Asahi tree)     the driver delta this port rebases onto Slackware's
                         own kernel source
  m1n1                   Apple Silicon bootloader
  u-boot (Asahi port)    UEFI environment
  asahi-scripts          update-m1n1, asahi-diagnose, asahi-fwupdate
  asahi-fwextract        vendor firmware extraction
  asahi-audio            PipeWire/WirePlumber DSP configuration
  alsa-ucm-conf-asahi    ALSA use-case configuration
  speakersafetyd         speaker protection daemon
  tiny-dfr               Touch Bar daemon


OTHER UPSTREAM PROJECTS PACKAGED HERE
-------------------------------------

  Mesa, PipeWire, lv2, lilv, serd, sord, sratom, zix, lsp-plugins,
  bankstown, triforce-lv2, lzfse.

Each is packaged as its authors released it, with the build flags recorded in
its SlackBuild. Where a package is a rebuild of one Slackware already ships,
the version is unchanged and only the build options differ.


